# Target C: close eight-no-root `k=6, D=-2, p=8` by functional-rank puncturing

Date: 2026-09-22

Status: rigorous closure of the remaining `D=-2` branch in the eight-no-root `k=6` layer. This uses the maximal replacement-functional rank proved in the immediately preceding reduction, a puncture-functoriality lemma for the canonical functional quotient, and already committed exact six- and five-row capacity/census certificates. It does not close the remaining `D=-1,p=9` side of the eight-no-root `k=6` layer, and it does not by itself close Target C-II or Erdős Problem #99.

